  <question type="coderunner">
    <name><text>S7 Q1 — Script stack machine</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #f7931a;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;">
<p style="color:#9a3412;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 8px;">S7 Q1 — Script stack machine</p>
<p style="color:#1e293b;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;margin:0;">Script processes tokens left to right on a stack: numbers are pushed, opcodes pop and push.</p>
</div>
<p style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;">Write <strong><code>eval_script(tokens)</code></strong>. Each token is a string. A numeric string is pushed (as an int). Support <code>OP_ADD</code>, <code>OP_SUB</code> (pop two, push a&minus;b in push order), <code>OP_DUP</code> (duplicate the top), and <code>OP_EQUAL</code> (push 1 if the top two are equal, else 0). Return the value on top of the stack.</p>
<div style="background:#fdf4ff;border-left:5px solid #9333ea;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 18px;margin:12px 0;">
<pre style="color:#3b0764;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:14px;margin:0;background:none;border:none;">eval_script(["2", "3", "OP_ADD"])   &rarr; 5
eval_script(["7", "OP_DUP", "OP_ADD"]) &rarr; 14</pre>
</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
