  <question type="coderunner">
    <name><text>S7 Q2 — Multisignature check</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #f7931a;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;">
<p style="color:#9a3412;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 8px;">S7 Q2 — Multisignature (m-of-n)</p>
<p style="color:#1e293b;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;margin:0;">A spend is valid only with at least m signatures from distinct listed keys.</p>
</div>
<p style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;">Write <strong><code>check_multisig(pubkeys, sigs, m)</code></strong>. Each element of <code>sigs</code> is the public key that produced it. A signature counts only if its key is in <code>pubkeys</code>. Return <code>True</code> if at least <code>m</code> <em>distinct</em> valid keys signed.</p>
<div style="background:#fdf4ff;border-left:5px solid #9333ea;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 18px;margin:12px 0;">
<pre style="color:#3b0764;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13px;margin:0;background:none;border:none;">check_multisig(["A","B","C"], ["A","B"], 2) &rarr; True
check_multisig(["A","B","C"], ["A","A"], 2) &rarr; False</pre>
</div>]]></text>
